/* book Worked example 2: Q: A tone x(t) = 2 cos(2π × 1.001 MHz × t) V is described about the reference carrier fc = 1 MHz. Find x̃(t), and the I and Q values at t = 0 and t = 0.125 ms.
   1. Write the tone as 2 cos(2π(fc + Δ)t) with offset Δ = 1.001 MHz − 1 MHz = 1 kHz.
   2. Analytic signal: xa(t) = 2ej2π(fc + Δ)t. Complex envelope: x̃(t) = 2ej2πΔt = 2cos(2π×10³t) + j2sin(2π×10³t) V.
   3. So xI(t) = 2cos(2π×10³t) and xQ(t) = 2sin(2π×10³t): the complex envelope turns round a circle of radius 2 V once per millisecond.
   4. At t = 0: I = 2 V, Q = 0.
   5. At t = 0.125 ms the angle is 2π × 10³ × 0.125×10−3 = π/4 = 45°, so I = 2 cos 45° = 1.414 V and Q = 2 sin 45° = 1.414 V. The envelope stays |x̃| = 2 V.
   Answer: x̃(t) = 2ej2π(1000)t V; at t = 0, (I, Q) = (2, 0) V; at t = 0.125 ms, (I, Q) = (1.414, 1.414) V. A frequency offset makes the complex envelope rotate at the offset frequency. */
