/* book Worked example: Q: White noise of two-sided PSD N0/2 = 1×10−6 W/Hz passes through an ideal low-pass filter of bandwidth B = 10 kHz and unit gain. Find the output PSD, the output power, the output autocorrelation RY(τ) and its first zero.
   1. Input PSD: SX(f) = 1×10−6 W/Hz at every f. Power gain |H(f)|² = 1 for |f| ≤ 10 kHz and 0 outside.
   2. Output PSD: SY(f) = 1×10−6 W/Hz for |f| ≤ 10 kHz, 0 outside: a rectangle 20 kHz wide.
   3. Output power = area of the rectangle = (1×10−6 W/Hz)(2 × 104 Hz) = 0.02 W = 20 mW. Check: N0B = (2×10−6)(104) = 0.02 W.
   4. Inverse transform of the rectangle (height S = 10−6, half-width B): RY(τ) = 2SB sinc(2Bτ) = 0.02 sinc(2×104τ) W.
   5. RY(0) = 20 mW, the power found in step 3. The first zero is at 2Bτ = 1, τ = 1/(2B) = 50 µs; further zeros at 100 µs, 150 µs and so on.
   Answer: SY(f) = 1×10−6 W/Hz for |f| ≤ 10 kHz; PY = 20 mW; RY(τ) = 20 mW × sinc(2×104τ), first zero at τ = 50 µs. */
