/* book exam traps: RX(0) is the average power E[X²], not the variance. The variance is RX(0) − μX²; they are equal only for a zero-mean process. | A two-sided PSD is integrated from −∞ to ∞; a one-sided PSD is twice as tall and integrated from 0. Mixing the two halves or doubles the answer. | The output PSD uses |H(f)|², not H(f). A filter with voltage gain 2 has power gain 4. | The autocorrelation of band-limited white noise is N0B sinc(2Bτ): its first zero is at 1/(2B), not 1/B. | Do not write SX(f) as |X(f)|² of one sample function. The PSD is the transform of the autocorrelation, an ensemble average. */
